.Dd October 16, 2024
.Dt ZERO 4
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm zero
.Nd source of zeroed memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/mman.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
device is a source of infinite zero bytes.
Reading from
.Nm
returns as many null characters (0x00) as requested.
Writing to
.Nm
discards the data and returns the number of bytes written.
.Pp
Memory mapping
.Nm
creates an anonymous zero-filled memory region. The mapping can be private (copy-on-write behavior) or shared (though behavior is effectively anonymous).
.Sh FILES
.Pa /dev/zero
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a 1MB zero-filled file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dd if=/dev/zero of=file.bin bs=1M count=1
.Ed
.Pp
Map anonymous memory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int fd = open("/dev/zero", O_RDWR);
void *ptr = mmap(NULL, 4096, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, 0);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr null 4 ,
.Xr full 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
device appeared in Substrate.
